# Known bug: Containment Priest judges whether a creature would enter by the card where it is (here the sorcery face in
# exile), not by the permanent as it would exist on the battlefield (CR 614.12), so a double-faced card put onto the
# battlefield transformed into a creature is not exiled (KI-47). Containment Priest's ruling: a noncreature card that
# wasn't cast and is entering the battlefield as a creature is exiled.
#
# "Exile it, then put it onto the battlefield transformed": Summon: Esper Maduin would enter as a nontoken creature that
# was not cast (the spell was Esper Origins; the permanent is put onto the battlefield by its effect, CR 712.14a), so
# Bot2's Containment Priest ("if a nontoken creature would enter and it wasn't cast, exile it instead") applies as it
# would enter (CR 614.12: the replacement looks at the back face it would have) and the card stays in exile. Nothing has
# entered, so nothing gets a finality counter and no chapter triggers. The surveil and the life still happened (24).

